("Can I sell a Concord house with repairs needed?","Yes. A cash buyer purchases as-is, and a conventional buyer can ask for repairs or a price cut after inspection. Get quotes first so you can compare the two outcomes."),
("Who collects property tax in Concord?","Cabarrus County collects it. The county office bills for the county, seven cities or towns and 16 fire districts, so the Concord rate arrives on one bill with the county rate."),
("Is there a deed tax when I sell in Concord?","Yes. North Carolina charges $1.00 per $500 or fractional part of the price, paid by the seller to the Register of Deeds before recording."),
